{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras","id":1519165,"title":"Your TC eras","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-30T05:15:15-07:00","id":1519165,"title":"Your TC eras","content":"Topic for loose brainstorming new Trinity Continuum eras.<br /> <br /> Here are mine ideas:<br /> 1. <b>Alchemy / Azo</b><b>th</b> - Alchemical era of 1500-1600s, with Dracula proposing Alchemy in their circles.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b2. <b>Afsana</b> / <b>Abbasside -</b> early Middle Ages era 700-900s. Golden Age of Islam, Carolingian Romance, beginning of Viking raids. Centered on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbasid_Caliphate\" target=\"_blank\">Abbasside Caliphate</a>. ( Think very much <b>Assassin's Creed: Mirage</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , name from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> )<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Avalon</b> - post-Roman British Isles and Justinian Byzantium\u200b circa 400-500s, with Arthurian fantasy and British mythology as its basis ( Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> for idea )<br /> <br /> EDIT: Quoting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> from page 3 of <b>eras ideas sum-up</b> to this date...<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis </b>official game in Late Bronze Collapse 1200-900 BCE.<br /> <br /> <b>Archon</b><b> / Auctoritas / Aurum</b> - proposed Roman Empire setting of 1st-5th century, probably a one book sub setting. ( alternative names from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> )\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Avalon </b>proposed Arthurian setting 400-500s, probably also a subsetting using <b>Aegis </b>rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Anathor </b>proposed early modern period (1500-1700) setting. Most likely using the <b>Adventure!</b> ruleset. ( And PIRATES in it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <b>A</b><b>ether</b> official game, victorian steampunk of 1890s.<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure! </b>official game, pulp adventure in 1920-1930s.<br /> <br /> <b>Atomic! </b>transitional between pulp and modern in 1940-1960s. ( See <b>'Oppenheimer'</b> movie and <b>They Came From Beneath the Sea</b> RPG. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <b>Aquarius </b>Psiads and conspiracies 1969-1999<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Core </b>&amp; <b>Assassins </b>'modern' official game setting. Action films in the present.<br /> <br /> <b>Adolescence - </b>a core book expansion about playing young adult characters, taking inspiration from things like Stranger Things, The Goonies, and the like.<br /> <br /> <b>Aberrant </b>official game, superheroes '10 years in the future' ( now like 2030s? ).<br /> <br /> <b>Anima </b>official game, cyberpunk and VR MMO in 2080s.<br /> <br /> <b>Aeon </b>\u200b\u200bofficial game, 'low' space opera in 2120s.<br /> <br /> <b>Argosy </b>proposed space opera setting. ( <b>WyrdH </b>- I would call it <b>Astra</b>)<br /> <br /> Outside of timeliness:<br /> <br /> <b>Agon</b> time war setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Ark </b>lost generation starship setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Axial </b>Planetary Romance setting on a lost human colony world.<br /> <br /> <b>Adnewyddu </b>alternate reality/timeline setting Arthur returns in a Post-apocalyptic Britain.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-10-2023, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:00:39-07:00","id":1519207,"title":"","content":"An alchemist's oven is called an <b>Anathor </b>(thanks <b>Dataweaver</b>). And I'd prefer the 1560 to 1660 period. The adventuring opportunities are just better. Mexico, Peru, Brazil, the Caribbean, North America, Japan, China, Europe, the Ottoman State, Persia, Mulghul India, the Dutch East Indies, Thailand, and a large number of African states are all in play. Piracy, Swashbuckling, Exploration, revolution (British Civil War, and several other interesting revolts) the Horror of the Thirty Years War, and Witch Hunting, all available in period.<br /> <br /> A conspiracy themed work on the 1940-1980 period seems viable, <b>Attention!</b>. Super Spies, UFO contactees, it would be more a transitional setting between Adventure! and the basic game.<br /> <br /> A far future game <b>Argosy</b> sometime after the year 3000AD. I'd want an over the top Space Opera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-31-2023, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:14:48-07:00","id":1519209,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a Time Travel setting, perhaps <b>Agon </b>(it means a struggle). It would be a time war setting involving different means of time travel.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see a planetary romance setting. It should be a human settled world that has only vague legends of the ancestors having crossed the skies from a distant star. The setting would be a world clawing its way back to civilization and the stars. <b>Axial </b>might be a good name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-30-2023, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T17:49:17-07:00","id":1519212,"title":"","content":"\u201cAthanor\u201d, not \u201cAnthor\u201d. Also, we will have a time travel \u201csetting\u201d very soon: the <b>Trinity Continuum Player's Guide</b> effectively gives us one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-21-2026, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T18:34:38-07:00","id":1519215,"title":"","content":"<b>Aquarius</b>, Psiads in the 1970s after the moon landing, where Armstrong and Aldren found and accidentally triggered an alien monolith. Featuring the \u00c6onic Institute for Psychic Studies.<br /> <br /> Inspired by Stephen King's early work (Carrie, Firestarter, The Dead Zone, The Shining), as well as things like Altered States, Scanners, The Fury, and to a lesser extent The Exorcist and The Omen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 07-30-2023, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T21:05:44-07:00","id":1519223,"title":"","content":"There were some fan talks about Ancient Rome one...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bArchon</b> - Imperial Rome of 1st till 5th century CE. Maybe more look on weird things going on with Roman Legions. ( Thanks <b>Astromancer</b> for name!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-31-2023, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T21:22:46-07:00","id":1519226,"title":"","content":"<b>Glamourweaver</b> on fan Discord proposed:<br /> <br /> Between <b>Aegis</b> and <b>Aether</b>:<br /> <br /> Alexander<br /> Arthur<br /> Afsaneh [Carolingian Romance and 1001 Nights]<br /> Acre [Third Crusade, Robin Hood\u2026]<br /> Azoth [Sun King, Pirates, Late Renaissance swashbuckling + alchemy]<br /> <br /> Post-<b>Adventure!:</b><br /> <br /> Atomic (50s-mid 60s)<br /> Action (70s-80s)\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T01:26:17-07:00","id":1519230,"title":"","content":"Aquarius seams an very solid setting. Phoebe Trust is a good start for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T02:55:34-07:00","id":1519234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519215#post1519215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aquarius</b>, Psiads in the 1970s after the moon landing, where Armstrong and Aldren found and accidentally triggered an alien monolith. Featuring the \u00c6onic Institute for Psychic Studies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is <b>monolith</b> showed before in TC? Was there official <b>\u00c6onic Institute for Psychic Studies</b>? Or o you only point that Stanley's Cubric <b>Odyssey 2001</b> and it's monolith scene was filmed in 1968?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cHWs3c3YNs4\" data-code=\"cHWs3c3YNs4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/cHWs3c3YNs4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T03:36:52-07:00","id":1519235,"title":"","content":"I took it as an idea for how the moon landing could be turned into a psi-based Hammersmith Event: say that Armstrong and Aldrin discover an alien artifact on the moon which then activates and floods the Earth with Noetic Energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T04:11:15-07:00","id":1519236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519223#post1519223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were some fan talks about Ancient Rome one...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bA</b><b>expension ( or Aempire</b>) - Imperial Rome of 1st till 5th century CE. Maybe more look on weird things going on with Roman Legions.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Archon</b> a word for a ruler seems good for Rome. And since the term is used for certain hostile spirits, hints at Rome's dark side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T05:22:02-07:00","id":1519241,"title":"","content":"Similarly, I might go with something like \u201cAstra\u201d for a far-future space opera setting. <br /> <br /> Also, my inclination would be to focus future setting books <i>after</i> Aether rather than <i>before</i> it, because there's not much Science to work with in earlier settings; and you essentially have to recast Super-Science as pseudo-magic in order to be able to do anything interesting with it. Which is fine in moderation, such as how Adventure and Aether over that as one possibility, or how one setting (Aegis) is probably going to mainstream it; but you don't want to overdo it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T10:33:36-07:00","id":1519265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519241#post1519241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similarly, I might go with something like \u201cAstra\u201d for a far-future space opera setting.<br /> <br /> Also, my inclination would be to focus future setting books <i>after</i> Aether rather than <i>before</i> it, because there's not much Science to work with in earlier settings; and you essentially have to recast Super-Science as pseudo-magic in order to be able to do anything interesting with it. Which is fine in moderation, such as how Adventure and Aether over that as one possibility, or how one setting (Aegis) is probably going to mainstream it; but you don't want to overdo it.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of <b>Anathor </b>I agree. Although the 2nd century AD is such a juicy period for adventure.<br /> <br /> A time travel game and a post 3000AD space opera setting would be the best.<br /> <br /> Many other proposed settings could be wonderful soucebooks for the Time Travel game. As several first edition books pointed out that INSPIRED PCs and low level Novas existed throughout human history but were vanishingly rare. This would allow all sorts of strange marvels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-31-2023, 06:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T13:15:32-07:00","id":1519278,"title":"","content":"Well, we've got all the mechanics we need for a time travel game (or we will, just as soon as TCPG comes out). In order to turn it into a full-on game, the other thing we need are Allegiances that specialize in world travel; and perhaps a ready-made source of conflict. The <s>Martians</s>Ascendancy(?) are still out there; though they seem to be more cross-world than time travel.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd go with <i>sourcebooks</i> for the time travel setting; but I could see <i>chapters in one sourcebook</i> for ideas that are interesting but aren't enough to develop into full books on their own. Call it the <b>Trinity Continuum Atlas</b>, maybe\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-21-2026, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T14:36:12-07:00","id":1519285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519235#post1519235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took it as an idea for how the moon landing could be turned into a psi-based Hammersmith Event: say that Armstrong and Aldrin discover an alien artifact on the moon which then activates and floods the Earth with Noetic Energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, yes. Said artifact could be either millions of years old or left behind in the wake of \u00c6ther. But it would flood the Earth with the necessary energy to start awakening Psiads who would be similar to what you see in the mentioned media as well as certain episodes of things like Wonder Woman and other 70s genre shows. (It would also signal whatever left the artifact, and possibly even have some sort of impact on Mars or other planets, assuming you wanted to work in aspects of things like Stranger in a Strange Land, various David Bowie works, or 70s UFO culture.)<br /> <br /> The \u00c6onic Institute for Psychic Studies I just made up, but I figure it would be part of the \u00c6on Society's evolution between the end of Adventure! and the beginning of the groups you see in the Trinity Continuum core book. <br /> You would probably also have a morally (dark) grey government group akin to the Shop from Firestarter, some sort of New Age religious movement, and a much more heroic government group similar to the ones from the Six Million Dollar Man/Bionic Woman and Wonder Woman. Certainly a few others as well.<br /> <br /> It would probably default to a 1974 or 1975 setting. Possibly with Nixon still being President.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:24:51-07:00","id":1519287,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that one of the Tasty Bits is a supplement about psions in the 20th and 21st centuries, complete with an organization dedicated to dealing with psychic phenomena. I'm forgetting it's name at the moment, though it's been mentioned in this thread; and I would expect it to be front and center in your 70s psychics setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:31:08-07:00","id":1519288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519278#post1519278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we've got all the mechanics we need for a time travel game (or we will, just as soon as TCPG comes out). In order to turn it into a full-on game, the other thing we need are Allegiances that specialize in world travel; and perhaps a ready-made source of conflict. The [s]Martians[/b]Ascendancy(?) are still out there; though they seem to be more cross-world than time travel.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'd go with <i>sourcebooks</i> for the time travel setting; but I could see <i>chapters in one sourcebook</i> for ideas that are interesting but aren't enough to develop into full books on their own. Call it the <b>Trinity Continuum Atlas</b>, maybe\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>A time travel game seems to scare you. Why?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:35:15-07:00","id":1519290,"title":"","content":"An interesting and fun &quot;one and done&quot; setting might be a lost generation starship. <b>Ark </b>perhaps? A vast artificial world would be an interesting and exotic setting. But one good book would cover the setting. I'd use a ruleset that allowed a wide variety of types. Probably like <b>Victorian Mage </b>it would use some other game's rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:46:40-07:00","id":1519292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519288#post1519288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A time travel game seems to scare you. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you think it scares me? I'm on board with it it's just that most of the work for one has already been done. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T15:57:37-07:00","id":1519294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519292#post1519292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you think it scares me? I'm on board with it it's just that most of the work for one has already been done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess I misread you.<br /> <br /> What do you think about <b>Ark </b>or <b>Axial</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T18:43:38-07:00","id":1519303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519287#post1519287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind that one of the Tasty Bits is a supplement about psions in the 20th and 21st centuries, complete with an organization dedicated to dealing with psychic phenomena. I'm forgetting it's name at the moment, though it's been mentioned in this thread; and I would expect it to be front and center in your 70s psychics setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm way behind on Tasty Bits. (I wish there was a convenient list of them divided by product line.) But yes, they would likely be part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Maybe also some sort of Psiad supremacy group as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T22:41:35-07:00","id":1519314,"title":"","content":"You mean <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/m/product/405547\" target=\"_blank\"><i><b>Pheobe Trust</b></i> Tasty Bit</a> - I used it in my modern 'Assassins protect non-binary Psiad' story I run last year. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> I also used it for backstory on my <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1487200-trinity-fan-era-cosmic-minds-psi-in-1950s-70s\"><i><b>Cosmic Minds</b></i> proto TC era</a>, which would be part of your <i><b>Aquarius</b></i> idea now - as it all notes on PSI goverment projects for in 50s-70s. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T17:42:43-07:00","id":1519384,"title":"","content":"Unrelated, <b>Avalon</b>, which would basically be the <i>\u00c6gis</i> set up transferred to post-Roman British Isles, with Arthurian fantasy and British mythology as its basis.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T18:49:57-07:00","id":1519390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519384#post1519384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated, <b>Avalon</b>, which would basically be the <i>\u00c6gis</i> set up transferred to post-Roman British Isles, with Arthurian fantasy and British mythology as its basis.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It could be a one off book with Merlin discovering a heretofore sealed supply of Ambrosia. Lancelot, Merlin, Ninue (the Lady of the Lake), Gawain, and Morgain would be Olympians, and maybe Sir Turquine. Players (the Knights and Damsels) would mainly be Champions with a few Oracles among the Damsels.<br /> <br /> Note: Damsel is a viable role. Read the stories, they were the medics, diplomats, and social operators. A knight without a skilled Damsel is generally going to be worse off than a damsel without a skilled Knight. The exceptions are over emphasized.<br /> <br /> Knights were overtrained and over focused on fighting and warfare. Everything else was the Damsel's job. Estate management, medicine, diplomacy, name it. Knights were normally illiterate until the later middle ages, women, priests, and commoners read.<br /> <br /> Merlin, Ninue, and Morgain, would have Oracle like powers as well as Olympian type ones. Alternatively the Lady of the Lake could be a manifestation of the crashed ship with the Ambrosia.<br /> <br /> By the way, this could set up a parallel universe outside the normal <b>Trinity </b>continuity where Arthur returns in a Post-apocalyptic Britain to save his people.<br /> <br /> <b>Adnewyddu, </b>a Welsh word for renewal might be a good name for this other one off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-02-2023, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T20:17:14-07:00","id":1519392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519390#post1519390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could be a one off book with Merlin discovering a heretofore sealed supply of Ambrosia. Lancelot, Merlin, Ninue (the Lady of the Lake), Gawain, and Morgain would be Olympians, and maybe Sir Turquine. Players (the Knights and Damsels) would mainly be Champions with a few Oracles among the Damsels.<br /> <br /> Note: Damsel is a viable role. Read the stories, they were the medics, diplomats, and social operators. A knight without a skilled Damsel is generally going to be worse off than a damsel without a skilled Knight. The exceptions are over emphasized.<br /> <br /> Knights were overtrained and over focused on fighting and warfare. Everything else was the Damsel's job. Estate management, medicine, diplomacy, name it. Knights were normally illiterate until the later middle ages, women, priests, and commoners read.<br /> <br /> Merlin, Ninue, and Morgain, would have Oracle like powers as well as Olympia type ones. Alternatively the Lady of the Lake could be a manifestation of the crashed ship with the Ambrosia.<br /> <br /> By the way, this could set up a parallel universe outside the normal <b>Trinity </b>continuity where Arthur returns in a Post-apocalyptic Britain to save his people.<br /> <br /> <b>Adnewyddu, </b>a Welsh word for renewal might be a good name for this other one off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think adhering to rigid social and gender roles for knights and damsels, even with the explanatory historical note you provided about how important damsels were to chivalric society, is sexist, but I won\u2019t tell you what to do in your own continuity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T03:18:23-07:00","id":1519405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519392#post1519392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think adhering to rigid social and gender roles for knights and damsels, even with the explanatory historical note you provided about how important damsels were to chivalric society, is sexist, but I won\u2019t tell you what to do in your own continuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, having women be knights was something even Medieval writers did. I'm saying ignoring the actual importance of damsels is sexist. I see no need to require males to be knights or females to be damsels. But the knight/damsel team dynamic deserves respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T04:22:08-07:00","id":1519408,"title":"","content":"If I were to try to develop Avalon into a full setting, various things like historical Briton/Celtic roles and medieval chivalric romance tropes would be part of the setting's basic cultural influences, but also the understanding that Champions and the like aren't really bound by such things, being special by their very nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T05:18:07-07:00","id":1519411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519408#post1519408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to try to develop Avalon into a full setting, various things like historical Briton/Celtic roles and medieval chivalric romance tropes would be part of the setting's basic cultural influences, but also the understanding that Champions and the like aren't really bound by such things, being special by their very nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already pointed out that Medieval writers did have female knights. I only wanted respect for the women who did a ton of work in Medieval society, the much maligned damsel. <br /> <br /> By the way, not only did fictional damsels like Lunette regularly save Knights in distress, but real world women did too. One of Eleanor of the Aquitaine's knights fell in a pond in late winter and was in danger of death by hypothermia. Eleanor, the ur damsel, hauled him out. <br /> <br /> The damsel role deserves respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T05:24:33-07:00","id":1519412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519405#post1519405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, having women be knights was something even Medieval writers did. I'm saying ignoring the actual importance of damsels is sexist. I see no need to require males to be knights or females to be damsels. But the knight/damsel team dynamic deserves respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, as long as you allow for female knights and male damsels and nonbinary members of either group, and as long as you allow for characters of any gender who aren\u2019t bound by the knight/damsel dichotomy, I agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T07:15:35-07:00","id":1519424,"title":"","content":"With Aquarius, I am sorely tempted for the \u00c6onic Institute to have a Mercer School for Gifted Youth that plays off a lot of the early X-Men material as a possible campaign.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T08:33:01-07:00","id":1519432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519424#post1519424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Aquarius, I am sorely tempted for the \u00c6onic Institute to have a Mercer School for Gifted Youth that plays off a lot of the early X-Men material as a possible campaign.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's sound <b>Aquarius </b>would be that place for aspects of Marvel Comics. Just as inspirations from DC silver age or Carlton Comics would fit best is a transitional setting between <b>Adventure! </b>and <b>Aquarius. </b> DC Golden age, Quality, and Faucet, all have more affinities with <b>Adventure! </b>than later periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T08:44:37-07:00","id":1519435,"title":"","content":"I think if you were doing <b>Atomic!</b> as a post WW2 setting - say about 1948 to 1962 - you would have to have at least one group that was clearly based on the sort of adventure science team archetype that gave us the Fantastic Four, the Challengers of the Unknown, the Sea Devils, and others. This might be the \u00c6on Society's role during the period.<br /> <br /> You'd also need a pre-movie, book era James Bond spy group. And a Godzilla homage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T16:08:15-07:00","id":1519521,"title":"","content":"What was Alan Moore's pulp pastiche character called? Had to google it: Tom Strong.<br /> <br /> That would fit that early Marvel/DC period of comics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T20:08:42-07:00","id":1519556,"title":"","content":"Aquarius Allegiances<br /> <br /> The \u00c6onic Institute for Psychic Studies<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The \u00c6on Society in this strange new world of 1974. They study and recruit Psiads as well as parapsychologists, cryptozoologists, and others devoted to studying unusual phenomenon.<br /> Among their organization is the Mercer School for Gifted Youth, a private school for Psiad children.</div> <br /> <br /> The Transcendent Alliance<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The group from the TC core book, who include former Axis scientists and Soviet defectors. They see Psiads as the obvious next stage in human evolution. Inspired by various parts of the movie Scanners (1981) as well as aspects of the early X-Men comics.</div> <br /> <br /> Office of Special Intelligence (OSI)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Branch 9 from the TC core book, currently getting a second wind thanks to the Psiad outbreak. Inspired by the Office of Scientific Intelligence (Six-Million Dollar Man/Bionic Woman) and the Inter-Agency Defense Command (Wonder Woman).</div> <br /> <br /> National Office of Special Research<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The National Office of Emergency Research from the TC core, just with an altered name. They work to contain, study, and harness the Psiad phenomenon for use by the US Government. Inspired by The Shop (Firestarter), ConSec (Scanners), and the real world SCANATE and Stargate projects.</div> <br /> <br /> Sphinx<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Pharaoh's Lightkeepers from the TC core, often recruiting Psiads for their mission teams. Inspired by Charlie's Angels, Mission: Impossible,</div> <br /> <br /> The Order of Cosmic Enlightenment<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A modern New Age religious movement (cult?) based around Psiads. Inspired by various period groups, especially in California (and to a certain degree the Church of Scientology).</div> <br /> <br /> Blackstar<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The Order of the Stars from Adventure, evolved into a Blaxspoitation style hero organization.</div> <br /> <br /> That's a baseline, at least. There'd likely be several others. Possibly an organized crime group tied to the Mafia, a martial arts organization, a talent agency that specializes in Psiad entertainers, a British or Interpol related spy group, and something based on Japanese sci fi of the period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:23:29-07:00","id":1519596,"title":"","content":"So, in my head, Aquarius generally defaults to around 1974 or 1975 as its default date, about five or six years after the Moon landing. Nixon is still President, as Watergate never happened. (Whatever they were looking for in the break in, they found it via NOSR supplied psychics using remote viewing ESP instead.) Nelson Rockefeller is the VP. By suppressing the Pentagon Papers and keeping up support for the South Vietnamese government after the withdrawal of U.S. troops, the Vietnam War, while not seen as a victory, isn't exactly viewed as a defeat either. The oil embargo has caused several Detroit automakers to experiment with new technology developed since the Moon landing. The Apollo Program continues alongside a much more ambitious Skylab project.<br /> <br /> While I think of Aquarius as having a strong focus on the US, especially California, obviously there is a lot going on elsewhere. Japan's economic boom, the Emperor of Ethiopia not being overthrown, South American N#zi holdovers, decolonialization, and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T04:23:35-07:00","id":1519597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519556#post1519556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aquarius Allegiances<br /> <br /> The \u00c6onic Institute for Psychic Studies<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The \u00c6on Society in this strange new world of 1974. They study and recruit Psiads as well as parapsychologists, cryptozoologists, and others devoted to studying unusual phenomenon.<br /> Among their organization is the Mercer School for Gifted Youth, a private school for Psiad children.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Transcendent Alliance<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The group from the TC core book, who include former Axis scientists and Soviet defectors. They see Psiads as the obvious next stage in human evolution. Inspired by various parts of the movie Scanners (1981) as well as aspects of the early X-Men comics.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Office of Special Intelligence (OSI)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Branch 9 from the TC core book, currently getting a second wind thanks to the Psiad outbreak. Inspired by the Office of Scientific Intelligence (Six-Million Dollar Man/Bionic Woman) and the Inter-Agency Defense Command (Wonder Woman).</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> National Office of Special Research<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The National Office of Emergency Research from the TC core, just with an altered name. They work to contain, study, and harness the Psiad phenomenon for use by the US Government. Inspired by The Shop (Firestarter), ConSec (Scanners), and the real world SCANATE and Stargate projects.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sphinx<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Pharaoh's Lightkeepers from the TC core, often recruiting Psiads for their mission teams. Inspired by Charlie's Angels, Mission: Impossible,</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Order of Cosmic Enlightenment<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">A modern New Age religious movement (cult?) based around Psiads. Inspired by various period groups, especially in California (and to a certain degree the Church of Scientology).</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Blackstar<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">The Order of the Stars from Adventure, evolved into a Blaxspoitation style hero organization.</div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's a baseline, at least. There'd likely be several others. Possibly an organized crime group tied to the Mafia, a martial arts organization, a talent agency that specializes in Psiad entertainers, a British or Interpol related spy group, and something based on Japanese sci fi of the period.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Deleted)\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 08-03-2023, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:41:02-07:00","id":1519616,"title":"","content":"Looking at what we got...<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis </b>official game.<br /> <br /> <b>Archon</b> proposed Roman setting, probably a one book sub setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Avalon </b>proposed Arthurian setting, probably also a subsetting using <b>Aegis </b>rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Anathor </b>proposed early modern period (1500-1700) setting. Most likely using the <b>Adventure!</b> ruleset.<br /> <br /> <b>A</b><b>ether</b> official game, steampunk.<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure! </b>official game, pulp adventure.<br /> <br /> <b>Atomic! </b>transitional between pulp and modern.<br /> <br /> <b>Aquarius </b>Psiads, and conspiracy 1969-1999<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Core </b>&amp; <b>Assassins </b>official game setting. Action films in the present. <br /> <br /> <b>Aberrant </b>official game.<br /> <br /> <b>Anima </b>official game<br /> <br /> <b>Aeon </b>\u200b\u200bofficial game.<br /> <br /> <b>Argosy </b>proposed space opera setting.<br /> <br /> Outside of timeliness.<br /> <br /> <b>Agon</b> time war setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Ark </b>lost generation starship setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Axial </b>Planetary Romance setting on a lost human colony world.<br /> <br /> <b>Adnewyddu </b>alternate reality/timeline setting Arthur returns in a Post-apocalyptic Britain.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think travel to alternative universes and general Post-apocalyptic settings are the only ones skipped. All other genres of Sci Fi and popular adventure literature are covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-03-2023, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:54:36-07:00","id":1519619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519596#post1519596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in my head, Aquarius generally defaults to around 1974 or 1975 as its default date, about five or six years after the Moon landing. Nixon is still President, as Watergate never happened. (Whatever they were looking for in the break in, they found it via NOSR supplied psychics using remote viewing ESP instead.) Nelson Rockefeller is the VP. By suppressing the Pentagon Papers and keeping up support for the South Vietnamese government after the withdrawal of U.S. troops, the Vietnam War, while not seen as a victory, isn't exactly viewed as a defeat either. The oil embargo has caused several Detroit automakers to experiment with new technology developed since the Moon landing. The Apollo Program continues alongside a much more ambitious Skylab project.<br /> <br /> While I think of Aquarius as having a strong focus on the US, especially California, obviously there is a lot going on elsewhere. Japan's economic boom, the Emperor of Ethiopia not being overthrown, South American N#zi holdovers, decolonialization, and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>1974-1975 was an interesting situation on South America too, not only the nazies, but also the dictatorship in many countries funded by the American government to prevent the spread of Communism. Killing students and all kinds of workers for being part of unions or spreading the ideas of Communism. It's a time with many secret and fallen heroes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T05:56:14-07:00","id":1519621,"title":"","content":"You also forgot the \u201ccore setting\u201d and Assassins. <br /> <br /> Some of the supposedly timeline settings aren't necessarily so. For instance, No One of Consequence has suggested that Aquarius should feature alterations to history such as the removal of Watergate and Nixon's humiliation \u2014 which would be a significant alteration to the timeline as we currently know it, though I suppose it doesn't <i>technically</i> alter anything in print. Still, as they describe it, Aquarius is borderline \u201calternate reality\u201d. <br /> <br /> Which is fine, given that we're talking with a Continuum here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T07:49:26-07:00","id":1519631,"title":"","content":"I'd probably describe Aquarius as 1970s New Age Sci Fi Psychic Weirdness.<br /> <br /> If you want some sort of out to return things to the basic timeline, then the monolith is a one-off discovery* and its energies dissipate by about 82 or so. Ted Kennedy is elected president in 1976 but is such a screw up that he crashes and drowns against Reagan in 1980. As that point, history becomes mostly what we know, with only a few alterations (certain tech areas are slightly altered, for example). <br /> <br /> At that point, the Continuum continues on with two separate things: <b>Action!</b> (@1986 or so, the over-the-top action movie genre of both Hollywood and Hong Kong, probably with basic core book rules augmented with some Assassins material) and <i>The Great 80s Time War</i>.<br /> <br /> Not sure what the 90s would involve. I'd say <i>Aliens</i>, but that name is taken.<br /> <br /> <br /> *At least until a giant second one is found orbiting one of the gas giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T13:28:54-07:00","id":1519658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519621#post1519621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also forgot the \u201ccore setting\u201d and Assassins.<br /> <br /> Some of the supposedly timeline settings aren't necessarily so. For instance, No One of Consequence has suggested that Aquarius should feature alterations to history such as the removal of Watergate and Nixon's humiliation \u2014 which would be a significant alteration to the timeline as we currently know it, though I suppose it doesn't <i>technically</i> alter anything in print. Still, as they describe it, Aquarius is borderline \u201calternate reality\u201d.<br /> <br /> Which is fine, given that we're talking with a Continuum here.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of parallel realities and <b>Reality Quakes</b> were the timeline mutates would between them allow for a wide variety of mini settings. My proposed settings of <b>Ark </b>&amp; <b>Adnewyddu </b>certainly don't fit the core timeline. But as alternative histories they fit in perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:24:25-07:00","id":1519665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519412#post1519412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, as long as you allow for female knights and male damsels and nonbinary members of either group, and as long as you allow for characters of any gender who aren\u2019t bound by the knight/damsel dichotomy, I agree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun side note Amethyst, J. Draper, a YouTube creator who's day job is Tour Guide in London, has found a possibily gender fluid person in 1300s London. John/Eleanor, they used both names, was a sex worker and embroider. They had male and female clients including Monks and Nuns.<br /> <br /> If one person, who seems gender fluid to our eyes, existed in 1300s London, and showed up in the records, there were probably others. How John/Eleanor defined themselves, we don't know. The court reporter stuck to the name John and exclusively used the male pronouns. Hey, it was the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> Still, John/Eleanor certainly shows nonbinary people in the period that created the Arthurian Romances that we read. (As opposed to long lost or hypothetical older texts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-04-2023, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T18:00:03-07:00","id":1519686,"title":"","content":"One of the later characters in Alan Moore's League of Extraordinary Gentlemen was Virginia Woolf's genderfluid immortal Orlando. While the original character's story starts in Elizabethan England, IIRC Moore makes the character both the Orlando from Shakespeare's As You Like It and the Paladin Orlando from the Italian versions of stories from The Song of Roland and The Matter of France. So I think it makes interesting character inspiration for Avalon (or some sort of Albion historical setting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T18:59:03-07:00","id":1519692,"title":"","content":"A slight nod to <b>TC Avalon</b> plot ideas - shannanigans of Merlin Ambrosius. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtube.com/shorts/zqk1EITDpXs?feature=share\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtube.com/shorts/zqk1EITDpXs?feature=share\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtube.com/shorts/zqk1EITDpXs?feature=share\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtube.com/shorts/zqk1EITDpXs?feature=share </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T20:03:41-07:00","id":1519703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1519665#post1519665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun side note Amethyst, J. Draper, a YouTube creator who's day job is Tour Guide in London, has found a possibility gender fluid person in 1300s London. John/Eleanor, they used both names, was a sex worker and embroider. They had male and female clients including Monks and Nuns.<br /> <br /> If one person, who seems gender fluid to our eyes, existed in 1300s London, and showed up in the records, there were probably others. How John/Eleanor defined themselves, we don't know. The court reporter stuck to the name John and exclusively used the male pronouns. Hey, it was the Middle Ages.<br /> <br /> Still, John/Eleanor certainly shows nonbinary people in the period that created the Arthurian Romances that we read. (As opposed to long lost or hypothetical older texts).</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating! Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T19:58:43-07:00","id":1519822,"title":"","content":"I'm going to start a thread on a Space Opera game in this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T20:05:03-07:00","id":1520169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras#post1519165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Archon</b> proposed Roman setting, probably a one book sub setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait\u2026 why would you use a term for an Athenian magistrate for a Roman Empire setting?<br /> <br /> some alternate options:<br /> <br /> Auctoritas - root of the English \u201cAuthority\u201d, refers to standing in Roman society, and even a numinous spiritual power to command<br /> <br /> Aurum - Latin for Gold","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 08-09-2023, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T03:27:24-07:00","id":1520179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520169#post1520169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait\u2026 why would you use a term for an Athenian magistrate for a Roman Empire setting?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The term was used in the Roman period by the Romans and had both positive and negative connotations. We have evidence that both illiterate and literate Romans knew the term. <br /> <br /> It may originate in Greece, but the word <b>Archon</b> was used as a Roman word. Also, any Roman game would involve both the positive and negative uses of power. <b>Archon </b>was used by the Romans to symbolize both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T04:10:28-07:00","id":1520181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520179#post1520179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The term was used in the Roman period by the Romans and had both positive and negative connotations. We have evidence that both illiterate and literate Romans knew the term.<br /> <br /> It may originate in Greece, but the word <b>Archon</b> was used as a Roman word. Also, any Roman game would involve both the positive and negative uses of power. <b>Archon </b>was used by the Romans to symbolize both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Greek was a commonly spoken language in the Empire, that doesn\u2019t make it a word closely associated with the empire itself. At most some Greek speakers used it to mean local governor. But more often it was used in the Eastern Empire to mean non-Roman king. So why use it as the title for a Roman Empire setting instead of a word more significant to Imperial Rome?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T05:26:54-07:00","id":1520186,"title":"","content":"<b>Adolescence</b>, a core book expansion about playing young adult characters, taking inspiration from things like Stranger Things, The Goonies, Zathura, Explorers, Monster Squad, and the like.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also Spy Kids. And various animated series I'm certainly forgetting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-09-2023, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T23:44:54-07:00","id":1520265,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> proposed on TC Discord - '<i><b>Afsana </b></i>(Golden Age of Islam, Carolingian Romance, beginning of Viking raids)' - I have question - What means <b>Afsana </b>exactly? Google is not showing me somehting concret on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T02:05:45-07:00","id":1520274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520265#post1520265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> proposed on TC Discord - '<i><b>Afsana </b></i>(Golden Age of Islam, Carolingian Romance, beginning of Viking raids)' - I have question - What means <b>Afsana </b>exactly? Google is not showing me somehting concret on this.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>\u0627\u0641\u0633\u0627\u0646\u0647 </b>or <i>afs\u00e2n</i> is apparently an old Persian word meaning story, fable, or legend. This would evoke <i>Hez\u00e2r Afs\u00e2ne</i>, The Thousand Tales, and sounds like something akin to \u00c6gis but focused on the Middle East, Persia, and North Africa, as well as the Indian Rim (Sri Lanka to Madagascar) and the Silk Road, with the lands of the Farangi and Northmen being far off and exotic.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T02:18:55-07:00","id":1520275,"title":"","content":"I keep trying to think of something to do with <i>Acadia</i>, the 17th and 18th century French settlements in Maine and the Maritime Provinces, but it always feels like something better suited for proto-Gothic horror than scifi adventure. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T14:48:47-07:00","id":1520321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520274#post1520274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>\u0627\u0641\u0633\u0627\u0646\u0647 </b>or <i>afs\u00e2n</i> is apparently an old Persian word meaning story, fable, or legend. This would evoke <i>Hez\u00e2r Afs\u00e2ne</i>, The Thousand Tales, and sounds like something akin to \u00c6gis but focused on the Middle East, Persia, and North Africa, as well as the Indian Rim (Sri Lanka to Madagascar) and the Silk Road, with the lands of the Farangi and Northmen being far off and exotic.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. The core setting would explore the proto-scifi and fantastical elements of 1001 Nights against the backdrop of the Golden Age of Islam under the reign of Harun Al-Rashid. The Afs\u00e2ne core setting book would probably include Christian (and pagan Norse) Europe to the same degree that Aegis features Sh\u0101ng China. But there would be room for Carolingian Romance and Viking Saga dedicated supplement books, just as Aegis totally has room for an Investiture of the Gods dedicated supplement book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T15:45:19-07:00","id":1520331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520321#post1520321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely. The core setting would explore the proto-scifi and fantastical elements of 1001 Nights against the backdrop of the Golden Age of Islam under the reign of Harun Al-Rashid. The Afs\u00e2ne core setting book would probably include Christian (and pagan Norse) Europe to the same degree that Aegis features Sh\u0101ng China. But there would be room for Carolingian Romance and Viking Saga dedicated supplement books, just as Aegis totally has room for an Investiture of the Gods dedicated supplement book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the major enchantments of the Arabian Nights are alchemical. So it isn't just proto-Sci Fi, it's often proto-science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T21:52:45-07:00","id":1520353,"title":"","content":"Well, speaking with Jinns instead of the dead sounds a lot like fairy tales, not S-F. \ud83d\ude0e But I assume <b>Afsana</b> is as much 'SgF under fantasy' setting - like <b>Aegis</b> is. \ud83d\ude0e Adding alchemy of era to it only grounding it more in S-F side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T22:08:41-07:00","id":1520354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520353#post1520353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, speaking with Jinns instead of the dead sounds a lot like fairy tales, not S-F. \ud83d\ude0e But I assume <b>Afsana</b> is as much 'SgF under fantasy' setting - like <b>Aegis</b> is. \ud83d\ude0e Adding alchemy of era to it only grounding it more in S-F side.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking since Champions and Oracles do so well simulating legendary heroes and magicians, that the setting might hinge on Abbasid or Tang Alchemists having discovered how to refine small amounts of Ambrosia (called something else) from inert remains from the Aegis era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T03:37:52-07:00","id":1520367,"title":"","content":"<b>Aegis </b>is a main setting. <b>Archon, Avalon </b>and <b>Afsana,</b> are all probably best done as setting books using the <b>Aegis </b>rule set. And, like <b>Dark Ages Mage</b>, also a one shot, if popular it gets sequels. That would lower the bar to getting the more distinctive settings. <br /> <br /> Note: The Doyne, as described in the <b>Aeon </b>game are very close to djinni, that is to say &quot;beings of smokeless fire&quot; would be a logical pre-scientific way to describe the Doyne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T04:48:01-07:00","id":1520374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520367#post1520367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: The Doyne, as described in the <b>Aeon </b>game are very close to djinni, that is to say &quot;beings of smokeless fire&quot; would be a logical pre-scientific way to describe the Doyne.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are totally right! Doyan as ancient Jinns! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Gona use it in my <b>Aeon</b> game!<br /> <br /> <img width=\"498\" height=\"339\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.tenor.com/nA1IBYf_E6IAAAAC/jaw-drop.gif\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/nA1IBYf_E6IAAAAC/jaw-drop.gif\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.tenor.com/nA1IBYf_E6IAAAAC/jaw-drop.gif\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T06:16:46-07:00","id":1520380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520367#post1520367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aegis </b>is a main setting. <b>Archon, Avalon </b>and <b>Afsana,</b> are all probably best done as setting books using the <b>Aegis </b>rule set. And, like <b>Dark Ages Mage</b>, also a one shot, if popular it gets sequels. That would lower the bar to getting the more distinctive settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my thought as well. Avalon would essentially just be the \u00c6gis rule set ported to a new setting. And my idea of an alchemy inspired setting (either the late 16th century or the time of Sir Isaac Newton) would basically use Aether's rules and ideas. The biggest issue with Aquarius is that it requires two books (\u00c6on and its \u00c6xpansion book) for Psiad rules.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T10:24:19-07:00","id":1520400,"title":"","content":"Hum...I'm unsure if it counts but I was thinking about a setting named &quot;Alterna&quot;. It's a massive futuristic city that exists in the flux and acts as a sanctuary for inspired who have lost their timelines due to an unknown phenomenon. These inspired consider themselves guardians of the multiverse and are searching for information as to how to stop this phenomenon and those who serve it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T11:56:41-07:00","id":1520402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520380#post1520380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my thought as well. Avalon would essentially just be the \u00c6gis rule set ported to a new setting. And my idea of an alchemy inspired setting (either the late 16th century or the time of Sir Isaac Newton) would basically use Aether's rules and ideas. The biggest issue with Aquarius is that it requires two books (\u00c6on and its \u00c6xpansion book) for Psiad rules.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t have strong thoughts on Aquarius as a concept, but the version I\u2019d make of Atomic (striding the Cold War from about 48 through the 60s) would feature early artificially stimulated psychomorphs with distinct mechanics from earlier Mesmerists or the post-Doyen-shield-fall Psiads. Lean into powers that are difficult to control, since that\u2019s a trope around psychic sci-fi that the Continuum hasn\u2019t really done yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T12:49:12-07:00","id":1520405,"title":"","content":"Speaking of using a game's rules for another setting, I keep poking at the idea of Atlantis as a sort of pre-historical (like around 4000 or 3000 BC or so maybe) thing where you have the island continent of Atlantis with 8 noble houses, each with its own Psion tank. So you have the Houses (each build around a different power set, but in a different way than the Orders), likely battling various Aberrants and their cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T18:36:21-07:00","id":1520422,"title":"","content":"<b>Alterna</b> would be a great setting book for a major factor in the time wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T15:55:03-07:00","id":1520553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520402#post1520402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t have strong thoughts on Aquarius as a concept, but the version I\u2019d make of Atomic (striding the Cold War from about 48 through the 60s) would feature early artificially stimulated psychomorphs with distinct mechanics from earlier Mesmerists or the post-Doyen-shield-fall Psiads. Lean into powers that are difficult to control, since that\u2019s a trope around psychic sci-fi that the Continuum hasn\u2019t really done yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Phoebe Trust</b> saddles modern psions with downsides, based on their generation. First generation psions suffer two complications that must be bought off with successes in order to avoid painful disorientation; second generation psions are dependant on chemical stimulants that are mildly poisonous; and third-generation psions need to attune themselves in order to use and maintain their powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T16:04:44-07:00","id":1520554,"title":"","content":"I think it might be interesting to try doing Atomics! using \u00c6ther's set up. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T16:25:07-07:00","id":1520557,"title":"","content":"Steve Jackson Games has a setting called GURPS Technomancer, where the premise is that Oppenheimer's quotation during the atomic bomb test accidentally completed a mystical ritual and turned the detonation into a dimensional gateway, letting magic flow into the world. I could see something very similar with \u201cAtomic!\u201d, except somewhat intended: while mostly forgotten, the age of Aether wasn't <i>completely</i> forgotten; and the Trinity Continuum counterpart to the Manhattan Project almost certainly included Talents and maybe even one or two Stalwarts; if any of them remembered the Aethergates, they might have co-opted the atomic bomb project to attempt to create a <i>new</i> Aethergate.<br /> <br /> The result likely wouldn't have been as dramatic as what happened in <b>GURPS Technomancer</b>; but I could definitely see it leading to a subsequent Aether-like Atomic Age. Only in the Atomic Age, it probably wouldn't be called Aether; instead, it would be viewed as some sort of nuclear by-product.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T17:29:44-07:00","id":1520561,"title":"","content":"Aether plus atomic radiation could allow kaiju for short periods. As the A-bombs were either used in Japan or tested in the American southwest (I'm speaking of the American A-bombs) it makes sense that these places are were the kaiju appear. Anywhere else and they aren't supported by the laws of physics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 08-14-2023, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T00:47:03-07:00","id":1520574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520557#post1520557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The result likely wouldn't have been as dramatic as what happened in <b>GURPS Technomancer</b>; but I could definitely see it leading to a subsequent Aether-like Atomic Age. Only in the Atomic Age, it probably wouldn't be called Aether; instead, it would be viewed as some sort of nuclear by-product.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are at <b>Atomic!</b> age of 1950-60s - new gates would surely open to worlds from S-F movies, comics and pulp magazines of the era! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Like <i><b>Forbidden Planet 1956</b></i><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AxQ9GG6hUDM\" data-code=\"AxQ9GG6hUDM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/AxQ9GG6hUDM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-14-2023, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T01:08:07-07:00","id":1520577,"title":"","content":"\u2026although I'd tend to place those gates in interplanetary space, accessed by Talent-built spacecraft, to capture the tendency of travel to other worlds in those works of fiction to mostly involve space travel. All of which fades from memory afterward for the same reason that the Aether Age faded in memory, leaving Neil Armstrong as the First Man on the Moon once the unwindings are completed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:09:26-07:00","id":1520624,"title":"","content":"Hmm, perhaps Atomic! might run from the July 1945 Trinity bomb test to the October 1962 nuclear war between the US and Soviets, ending in an unwinding similar to that of \u00c6ther.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:38:10-07:00","id":1520630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1520624#post1520624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, perhaps Atomic! might run from the July 1945 Trinity bomb test to the October 1962 nuclear war between the US and Soviets, ending in an unwinding similar to that of \u00c6ther.</div> </div> </div> </div>With an <i><b>Unwinding </b></i>that opens the possibilities. The Roswell incident could involve a crashed saucer. Space adventures and colonization could happen. If the <b><i>\u200b\u200bUnwinding </i></b>was limited to the solar system, anomalous ruined bases and colonies, failed or otherwise, could be around for either <b>Aberrant </b>or <b>Aeon</b>. <br /> <br /> The concept of the &quot;<i>Pragmaclapse</i>&quot; could both justify <b>Aquarius </b>and leave mysterious clues for <b>Aberrant</b>, <b>Anima </b>and <b>Aeon. </b>A <i>Pragmaclapse </i>is a being or object leftover from a reality that no longer exists. A second <b><i>Unwinding </i></b>in less than a millennium would scatter <i>Pragmaclapses </i>as far and wide as the Storyteller would like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T17:11:14-07:00","id":1520633,"title":"","content":"It's interesting (to me, at least), that the early 60s gives us three atomic derived superheros. Captain Atom from 1960 (the character that would later be adapted into Dr. Manhattan for the Watchmen), the Incredible Hulk in early 1962, and Doctor Solar, Man of the Atom in late 1962. I think you have several interesting ideas for whatever you would call the Atomic! equivalent to Magogs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, of course, Godzilla (54), Anguirus (55), Rodan (56), and Mothra (61).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-14-2023, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T03:18:23-07:00","id":1521499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras#post1519165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b2. <b>Afsana</b> / <b>Abbasside -</b> early Middle Ages era 700-900s. Golden Age of Islam, Carolingian Romance, beginning of Viking raids. Centered on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abbasid_Caliphate\" target=\"_blank\">Abbasside Caliphate</a>. ( Think very much <b>Assassin's Creed: Mirage</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , name from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> )<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>First and Fourth Season of <i><b>Echoes of History</b></i> - historical reaserch podcast for <b>Assassin's Creed</b> series - have great stuff for our <b><i>Afsana</i></b> era and it's Abbasside Caliphate and Viking raids backgrounds! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-rq9ha-1a4047e0?utm_campaign=w_share_ep&amp;utm_medium=dlink&amp;utm_source=w_share\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/63d94883bacb1e0011b6409c/1692000768917-1e397cc45be9215f265214199d0d217c.jpeg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-rq9ha-1a4047e0?utm_campaign=w_share_ep&amp;utm_medium=dlink&amp;utm_source=w_share\" target=\"_blank\"> Baghdad Soundwalks | Trailer </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-rq9ha-1a4047e0?utm_campaign=w_share_ep&amp;utm_medium=dlink&amp;utm_source=w_share\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.podbean.com/media/share/dir-rq9ha-1a4047e0?utm_campaign=w_share_ep&amp;utm_medium=dlink&amp;utm_source=w_share </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Baghdad Soundwalks guides you through the history, intrigue and drama of medieval Baghdad, the setting for Assassin's Creed Mirage. Join our hosts Ali A Olomi and Deana Hassanein as they explore an exciting time period which is often overlooked. An original Ubisoft series, produced by Paradiso Media.First episode drops October 21. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T11:31:47-07:00","id":1521521,"title":"","content":"Alternate timelines seem like a good source for one shot books.<br /> <br /> Try an alien invasion in the late middle ages. The aliens assume humans are helpless. The aliens then learn better. <br /> <br /> A plague in the 1930s collapses civilization. It is now the present and humanity is rebuilding. <br /> <br /> Pirates in the 1690s discover Ambrosia. Hilarity ensues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T13:50:00-07:00","id":1521530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1521521#post1521521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternate timelines seem like a good source for one shot books.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I keep fiddling with the idea of an alternate timeline where Germany won WW1 fairly quickly, possibly because of Talants and/or time travelers making minor alterations around the start of the century that among other things prevent Britain from joining the war. I'm just not sure what to do with it. Maybe an alternate pulp Adventure setting in the 30s, or possibly some sort of Cold War-esque thing with Assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T10:24:54-07:00","id":1521601,"title":"","content":"With a quick victory in WWI, you don't get the crushing reparations that Germany was made to endure in our timeline; which in turn means no fall of the Weimar Republic, no rise of Hitler and the Nazis, and no WWII. For that matter, a quick WWI victory would have ended the war before the US got into it; and you wouldn't even get as much of the horrors of trench warfare. It wouldn't be World War I, and probably wouldn't even be The Great War; it might just be \u201cthe War in Europe\u201d. <br /> <br /> The latter half of the 20th century was shaped by the World Wars; without them, the world would end up looking very different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T11:35:38-07:00","id":1521607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1521601#post1521601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a quick victory in WWI, you don't get the crushing reparations that Germany was made to endure in our timeline; which in turn means no fall of the Weimar Republic, no rise of Hitler and the Nazis, and no WWII. For that matter, a quick WWI victory would have ended the war before the US got into it; and you wouldn't even get as much of the horrors of trench warfare. It wouldn't be World War I, and probably wouldn't even be The Great War; it might just be \u201cthe War in Europe\u201d.<br /> <br /> The latter half of the 20th century was shaped by the World Wars; without them, the world would end up looking very different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly the European monarchies would last longer. Much of the rapid social change we saw in the 20th century came from the total deligitimation of traditional society in the face of the world wars and the constant threat of nuclear war after the 1940s. <br /> <br /> Technology would probably progress more slowly. <br /> <br /> With a quick victory in WWI the Russian revolution becomes less likely. Without the Russian Revolution the Red Scares in the USA become less likely. Socialism, which hobbled itself in America, might get a chance in the US. So you might continue the 19th century pattern of a conservative Europe and a radical America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T18:23:28-07:00","id":1521634,"title":"","content":"My initial thinking is that, For Reasons\u2122, there never is a naval arms race between Britain and Germany, lowering the tension between the two powers. Germany instead uses that money on the army, and instead of going through Belgium, manages to fight through the French forces at the border and eventually take Paris. The French capitulate, and only end up losing a few of their African colonies and a couple of Pacific islands in the treaty. But it's enough to eventually make the Republic fall. And Paris may be the new hotness for international Marxism.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Eastern front is more of a slog, but the Russians eventually lose. Finland, Poland-Lithuania, and Ukraine are established as buffer states/puppets, and the Revolution happens, but Lenin is still sitting in a German jail, so the Bolsheviks never come to power. Russia is probably a weak and corrupt Constitutional Monarchy for the next few decades.<br /> <br /> Austria-Hungary could perhaps try to evolve into a Tripple Monarchy (adding Serbia), but the early 20th century European obsession with ethnic nationalism will likely tear it apart regardless. <br /> <br /> In the US, Wilson doesn't get reelected. I'm still working on specifics for it, as well as what happens in the Middle East, Japan, China, Mexico, Britain, and Ireland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T12:03:39-07:00","id":1521685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1521530#post1521530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I keep fiddling with the idea of an alternate timeline where Germany won WW1 fairly quickly, possibly because of Talants and/or time travelers making minor alterations around the start of the century that among other things prevent Britain from joining the war. I'm just not sure what to do with it. Maybe an alternate pulp Adventure setting in the 30s, or possibly some sort of Cold War-esque thing with Assassins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you heard about <a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kaiserreich_Wiki?\" target=\"_blank\">https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/...serreich_Wiki?</a> I've considered running a game of adventure in such a setting, the people developing the world have done an amazing job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T13:40:01-07:00","id":1521692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1521685#post1521685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you heard about <a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kaiserreich_Wiki?\" target=\"_blank\">https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/...serreich_Wiki?</a> I've considered running a game of adventure in such a setting, the people developing the world have done an amazing job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard of Kaiserreich, but am not overly familiar with it. Thank you for the link as it gives me a number of historical points to poke around at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T17:45:17-07:00","id":1521794,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Kaiserreich timeline, I am reminded about Irish home rule (and certain matters with the Welsh church) being delayed because of the War. So, in this hypothetical setting, that delay doesn't happen, and Ireland gets its own Parliament. This means no Easter Uprising, and the Irish independence movement probably still being mainly focused on legal maneuvering rather than violent rebellion. (Although, things being what they are, there's probably going to be outbreaks of violence in the north that may eventually require Ulster being split off on its own anyway.) <br /> <br /> I want the Ottoman Empire to still collapse, possibly because of civil war (likely between the Committee of Union and Progress and more traditionalist factions that grows to include the various ethnic independence movements) and other factors. The UK and Germany probably broker and enforce a peace treaty of some sort. I'm thinking that Constantinople and the surrounding Bosporus Straight become and international zone, full of various intrigues, spies, smugglers, and other fun adventure/espionage tropes. There's a Turkish state in much of Anatolia, but also a larger independent Armenia in the east along with an independent Kurdistan. Much of Mesopotamia and the Arabian Peninsula are ruled by the Hashemite Kingdom (that may or may not declare itself the new Caliphate). Palestine is a German protectorate. Kuwait and Oman are under British influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-02T07:41:50-07:00","id":1521872,"title":"","content":"The reason why I like the Kaiserreich timeline so much is because their political ideologies and national landscape have a lot more shades of grey than our world. Without the extremism of Stalinism in the soviet union and the pure evil of the nazis, democracy is not necessarily considered the standard &quot;good&quot; system and the only viable option, even though some ideologies are clearly more oppressive than others (<a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_Political_Ideologies\" target=\"_blank\">https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/...cal_Ideologies</a>). What this would mean for the adventure setting is that the political inclinations of the characters would play a much bigger part. For example, I could see another internal division within the AEON Society that is purely about politics in which the most idealistic members constantly argue about which political system should set the path to the future. Maxwell then would have to decide if he should pick a side and risk losing members who could create more radical organizations, or try to appease everyone at the cost of stability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-04T16:26:33-08:00","id":1526335,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that <b>Alterna </b>could be a Trinityverse equivalent to Tanelorn from Moorcock's multiverse. Tanelorn was present in every world of Moorcock's multiverse if only as an idea or a fiction.<br /> <br /> In the <b>Avalon </b>and <b>Abnewyddu</b> settings it might be present as the Castle of the Border or the Spiral Castle. In <b>Afsana </b>it could be Baghdad itself. In later settings it could be a comic book series or a fantasy novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-04-2023, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T13:49:03-08:00","id":1526370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1526335#post1526335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In later settings it could be a comic book series or a fantasy novel.</div> </div> </div> </div>In \u00c6ther, a private club.<br /> <br /> In Adventure!, one of the early pulp science fiction magazines.<br /> <br /> In Aquarius, a VW microbus that is bigger on the inside than outside, driven by a mysterious man known only as &quot;The Wizard&quot;, accompanied by his odd companions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T23:42:44-08:00","id":1526796,"title":"","content":"I have been poking around at the idea of Assassins in Aquarius, drawing on things like CURE (the Remo Williams/Destroyer novels), SPECTRE (Bond books and films), C2 (The Eiger Sanction), Day of the Jackyl, and Golgo 13 among other influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T04:59:21-08:00","id":1526801,"title":"","content":"Assassins in Aquarius is basically the spy movies of the 70s. You just slow down a bit on the killing and give them a bit more government funding.<br /> <br /> Also, for sure the super powers (USSR and USA), not to say most of the countries, have some deal in the shadow\u2026 come on, is there anything more shade than CIA x KGB?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T09:38:43-08:00","id":1526809,"title":"","content":"With the exception of SPECTRE (who are a third party trying to pit the East and West against each other so that they can then swoop in and eliminate the surviving side and take control) and Christopher Lee's portrayal of Scaramonga, I'm really looking more at the luridly violent pulp novel series of the decade. Things like The Destroyer, The Executioner, The Baroness, The Death Merchant, and Killmaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T19:51:09-08:00","id":1526892,"title":"","content":"Assassin group concepts in Aquarius (none of these are named, and there are probably preexisting groups which can be slotted into these roles; I just don't have any books handy to check at the moment). <br /> <br /> The Western Star Chamber - nominally American, but possibly also including other NATO members and allies. The super secretive agency that in theory answer only to the President, but in all likelihood are a law unto themselves. How &quot;honorable&quot; they are would really depend on just who is in charge. A Wilford Brimley lookalike working an anonymous job in a bank basement who truly believes in American ideals is going to run a different shop than a psychotic albino kept alive via blood transfusions from orphans. Their targets are those threats to Freedom/Queen &amp; Country, but whose existence can't be exposed to the public or even most normal government offices. <br /> <br /> The Third Party - The middle faction in the Cold War, who seek to play both sides against each other in order to weaken them and eventually knock off the winner. Exactly what their motivations and post-victory plans might vary, from world domination to some sort of idealistic &quot;greater good&quot; utopia (that like most utopias ends up being build on the corpses of anyone in the way.<br /> <br /> The Ladies Finishing School for Assassins - The femme fatals, motivated by a mix of thrill seeking, profit, liberation, and group loyalty. <br /> <br /> The Hunt Club - the thrill seekers who do this for fun (and a lot of money). <br /> <br /> The Octopus - The Man, aka the People in Power and their agents working to advance their way up the ladder. Essentially killing to maintain the status quo and their place in it. <br /> <br /> The Ancient Order of Assassins - The &quot;exotic Orientals&quot;, drawing on Ra's al Ghul's sect from the 1970s Batman comics and Fu Manchu in Marvel's Master of Kung Fu, as well as all of the other period material that influenced them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T02:49:01-08:00","id":1526972,"title":"","content":"Doing Scandia's Aesir (Olympians) in <b>Aegis </b>or <b>Afsana </b>eras - What high level Inteligence Olympian from North looks like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YoJR_VjorTg\" data-code=\"YoJR_VjorTg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YoJR_VjorTg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-06T07:52:13-07:00","id":1538170,"title":"","content":"An interesting faction in the time wars might be a group who's history was completely erased. Unlike Atlantis or Tanelorn it doesn't even exist as a myth or fiction. This group might fanatically hunt down all pragmaclapses in a desperate struggle to reconnect with their reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T13:24:30-08:00","id":1548480,"title":"","content":"Steam Wars suggests that the alternate realities possible are fairly extravagant. And more importantly, like Steam Wars, can overlap existing settings. <br /> <br /> We really need a mid century America where airships make every town a port city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-16T14:31:17-08:00","id":1548537,"title":"","content":"<b>Aero </b>would be a game setting using the <b>Adventure! </b>rules set in an alternate mid20th century were giant airships dominate transcontinental travel. It would draw on Pulp seafaring stories, Kipling's &quot;<b>With the Night Mail&quot; </b>and &quot;<b>Easy as ABC&quot; </b>and Michael Moorcock's &quot;<b>Warlord of the Air.&quot;</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-16-2025, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T09:41:35-08:00","id":1548586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548537#post1548537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aero </b>would be a game setting using the <b>Adventure! </b>rules set in an alternate mid20th century were giant airships dominate transcontinental travel. It would draw on Pulp seafaring stories, Kipling's &quot;<b>With the Night Mail&quot; </b>and &quot;<b>Easy as ABC&quot; </b>and Michael Moorcock's &quot;<b>Warlord of the Air.&quot;</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also the old Crimson Skies game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T18:36:08-08:00","id":1548722,"title":"","content":"We need a game focused on the Tokusatu (sic) genre. It should use the <b>Adventure! </b>rules. However certain details of genre would alter how some rules work. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T23:23:40-08:00","id":1548726,"title":"","content":"Are you sure that shouldn't be a They Came From product?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T07:59:32-08:00","id":1548731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548726#post1548726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure that shouldn't be a They Came From product?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguments could be made both ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T08:05:51-08:00","id":1548732,"title":"","content":"Given <b>Steamwars</b> overlaps both <b>Aether </b>and <b>Adventure! </b>there is room for a Golden Age Sci Fi game drawing on 40s and 50s Sci Fi 50s B-films, Star Trek OS, Classic Doctor Who's first four Doctors, and the British Scientific Romance genre post WWII. Something with a Jetsons/1960s World's Fair Futurama look to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-05-2026, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T17:57:08-08:00","id":1548743,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the idea of not using TC for a game and instead use TCF is a bit silly.<br /> The genre being simulated can be explored by both, but the general feeling of the result is different.<br /> <br /> TC brings a more solid set of rules, so you can explore the rules to gain advantage, be you the Storyguide or a player. While not exactly tactical, the system gives limits on the uses the supernatural powers, while equipment have a greater impact in the game play.<br /> TCF is much more lose in their way, you character can do stuff, what exactly is up to the situation. The powers are really lose ended and the equipment is all improvised. I think, to my taste, TCF has a weak version of the SP, too lose to my taste and with little concern about how to deal with scale for example.<br /> Scion, while open ended, has far more solid system for equipment and powers, that TCF lacks completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-24T06:34:08-08:00","id":1548751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548743#post1548743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the idea of not using TC for a game and instead use TCF is a bit silly.<br /> The genre being simulated can be explored by both, but the general feeling of the result is different.<br /> <br /> TC brings a more solid set of rules, so you can explore the rules to gain advantage, be you the Storyguide or a player. While not exactly tactical, the system gives limits on the uses the supernatural powers, while equipment have a greater impact in the game play.<br /> TCF is much more lose in their way, you character can do stuff, what exactly is up to the situation. The powers are really lose ended and the equipment is all improvised. I think, to my taste, TCF has a weak version of the SP, too lose to my taste and with little concern about how to deal with scale for example.<br /> Scion, while open ended, has far more solid system for equipment and powers, that TCF lacks completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I\u2019m much more of a lore person than I am a rules person, I still prefer the feel of the Trinity Continuum setting to that of They Came From\u2026.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-27T15:30:45-08:00","id":1548806,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering something along the lines of &quot;the many facets of the 1970s&quot;. I've previously mentioned <i>Aquarius</i> as the idea of a psychic centered 70s setting, and I have also long used Adventure! as a way to do the heroes of 1970s adventure and genre television (Charlie's Angels, The Bionic Woman, Wonder Woman, etc.), but I feel there may be others. I'm not sure about a full blown Nova outbreak, as I have yet to figure out a way to make it distinctively 70s. I'm also still mulling over way \u00c6ther or \u00c6gis might translate to the period. (Anima seems to be something that might work in the early 80s, drawing heavily on Tron.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T03:57:45-08:00","id":1548812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548806#post1548806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pondering something along the lines of &quot;the many facets of the 1970s&quot;. I've previously mentioned <i>Aquarius</i> as the idea of a psychic centered 70s setting, and I have also long used Adventure! as a way to do the heroes of 1970s adventure and genre television (Charlie's Angels, The Bionic Woman, Wonder Woman, etc.), but I feel there may be others. I'm not sure about a full blown Nova outbreak, as I have yet to figure out a way to make it distinctively 70s. I'm also still mulling over way \u00c6ther or \u00c6gis might translate to the period. (Anima seems to be something that might work in the early 80s, drawing heavily on Tron.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonder Woman in the 70s TV show wasn't as powerful as she has normally been in the comics. The Linda Carter Wonder Woman could be handled with the <b>Adventure! </b>rules. The Bionic Woman and the Six Million Dollar Man could be handled similarly.<br /> <br /> Also, it's cannon that there were Novas before Divis Mal stepped in to force the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T05:13:06-08:00","id":1548814,"title":"","content":"As I see, the difference between a Stalwart and a Nova is within 2 limits.<br /> - Stalwarts are the way they are in Adventure because they are in a high Flux environment, while thir quantum powers are limited by external force.<br /> - Stalwarts have little to no knowledge of their powers workings, and so they can\u2019t develop their powers as easily as a post N-Day Nova (or a Terat that has worked with Mal during the years prior N-Day).<br /> <br /> After the end of Adventure! Era, Stalwarts lost part of their powers, not the quantum part, but the Dramatic Editing Part, as the environment flux level reduced to \u201cnormal\u201d. And until N-Day they were still limited by the external effect, that Mal ended.<br /> <br /> My suggestion for playing a game in the 60-80s is using Adventure! rules with a few changes. Removing the DE capacity of Stalwarts and Mesmerists and use Talents instead of Daredevils (no big differences). The exclusive DE of Stalwarts and Mesmerists (basically access to Max Out and Reaching, form Aberrant and Aeon eras) are stainless available and costs 1 Inspiration. It covers the combination of Action Heroes and low level Super Powers without mixing too much the arenas of each of the templates.<br /> <br /> Edit: A suggestion is to use my Powered Inspiration rules in my signature. I mean, they are a variation of Adventure Rules to reach full Novas and Psions/Psiads, and they can toned up and down according to the level of power you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-28-2025, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T06:55:42-08:00","id":1548815,"title":"","content":"Most of the superhumans from 70s TV would fall under the category of Stalwarts for this. Wonder Woman, the Man from Atlantis, The Six Million Dollar Man and Bionic Woman, The Incredible Hulk, Bigfoot, and characters from things like Future Cop or The Immortal, among others. (Also the TV versions of Spiderman and Captain America.)<br /> <br /> Daredevils would be various cop/detective characters, as well as Charlie's Angels, the three leads from Enter the Dragon, The Executioner, Evel Knevel, The Magician, and the Roger Moore era James Bond, to name a few. (Also probably the post-tv era Batman aka The Hairy Chested Love God, that tended to bounce between gothic horror and international intrigue.)<br /> <br /> Mesmerists are also pretty common, appearing in several of the above shows as one off characters. Plus period fiction like some of Stephen King's early work (Carrie, The Shining) and the TV Doctor Strange.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure how to classify things like Captain Marvel, Isis, or Doctor Who.<br /> <br /> But none of this would be a full Nova setting using Aberrant. I'm not sure what something like that would look like. At least some of it might draw on the Satellite Era JLA and some bits of the early All New All Different X-Men. But I would also have to look at some period sci fi and anime for ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T11:09:16-08:00","id":1548818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548815#post1548815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the superhumans from 70s TV would fall under the category of Stalwarts for this. Wonder Woman, the Man from Atlantis, The Six Million Dollar Man and Bionic Woman, The Incredible Hulk, Bigfoot, and characters from things like Future Cop or The Immortal, among others. (Also the TV versions of Spiderman and Captain America.)<br /> <br /> Daredevils would be various cop/detective characters, as well as Charlie's Angels, the three leads from Enter the Dragon, The Executioner, Evel Knevel, The Magician, and the Roger Moore era James Bond, to name a few. (Also probably the post-tv era Batman aka The Hairy Chested Love God, that tended to bounce between gothic horror and international intrigue.)<br /> <br /> Mesmerists are also pretty common, appearing in several of the above shows as one off characters. Plus period fiction like some of Stephen King's early work (Carrie, The Shining) and the TV Doctor Strange.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure how to classify things like Captain Marvel, Isis, or Doctor Who.<br /> <br /> But none of this would be a full Nova setting using Aberrant. I'm not sure what something like that would look like. At least some of it might draw on the Satellite Era JLA and some bits of the early All New All Different X-Men. But I would also have to look at some period sci fi and anime for ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>As depicted, both Captain Marvel and Isis are Nova level. Myself, I'd say that comic book Wonder Woman, and TV Captain Marvel and Isis are all Scions. That's another game though. As to Doctor Who and Captain Scarlett, they're both Novas. Even their weakest versions go beyond Stalwarts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T23:21:45-08:00","id":1548937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548818#post1548818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Myself, I'd say that comic book Wonder Woman, and TV Captain Marvel and Isis are all Scions. That's another game though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where TC:Aegis comes in: it's built around the reframing of Quantum and Psi heroes as demigods and mystics, and recasting Flux effects as the workings of Fate: Twists of Fate, Mighty Oaths, Dire Portents, and Invoking the Moirai. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T11:58:35-08:00","id":1548962,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering the idea of the so-called New Wave of science fiction from the 60s and 70s as a focus for a 1970s \u00c6ther, drawing on various ideas from people like Moorcock, Elison, and Dick, among others. Such a thing would probably get very weird very fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T14:59:45-08:00","id":1548968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1548962#post1548962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pondering the idea of the so-called New Wave of science fiction from the 60s and 70s as a focus for a 1970s \u00c6ther, drawing on various ideas from people like Moorcock, Elison, and Dick, among others. Such a thing would probably get very weird very fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Groovy Man! (And yes, I am old enough to have said &quot;Groovy&quot; without irony. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-05T11:59:55-08:00","id":1548986,"title":"","content":"I still don't really have an idea for what \u00c6gis and its ambrosia exploding all over the 1970s would look like. On the one hand, there might be something interesting to be done with period mythology involving UFOs and the silly ancient astronauts idea, but I think my concept for Aquarius already touches on that. Another possibility would be to play off period environmentalism with &quot;ambrosia&quot; (or whatever its stand in is) creating mutated monsters from nature (in the vein of The Prophecy or the early Swamp Thing and Man-Thing comics) while also creating heroes akin to the X-Men and various misfits. Although that might work better as a late 80s setting that just goes full on TMNT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-07T22:56:28-08:00","id":1549067,"title":"","content":"The main setting of Aberrant but further along the timeline and maybe going into a different future track.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-15T03:40:09-07:00","id":1553833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1549067#post1549067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main setting of Aberrant but further along the timeline and maybe going into a different future track.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legion of Superheroes could be fun. But I would like to raid <b>Kamandi </b>and <b>Thundarr the Barbarian!</b> Supers in a post-apocalyptic setting. Basically the <b>Adventure! </b>ruleset with more points (these characters are more powerful, but not that much more powerful) set in a very Golden Age Sci Fi setting. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T09:18:53-07:00","id":1553875,"title":"","content":"Hmm... <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/joypixels/assets/8.0/png/unicode/64/1f914.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/joypixels/assets/8.0/png/unicode/64/1f914.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/joypixels/assets/8.0/png/unicode/64/1f914.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse Then</b>, based on a bunch of the post-apocalyptic media of the 70s, 80s, and 90s.<br /> <br /> Primary Influences: The Road Warrior, Mad Max: Beyond Thunderdome, Thundarr the Barbarian, TMNT: After the Bomb, Cadillacs &amp; Dinosaurs, The Omega Man, Komandi, Tank Girl, Killraven, The Atomic Knights.<br /> <br /> Secondary Influences: Rifts, Terminator and Terminator 2, Damnation Alley, Logan's Run, Zardoz, the original Planet of the Apes franchise, Waterworld, The Postman, Cyborg, Six String Samurai, Hell Comes to Frogtown, 12 Monkeys, A Canticle for Leibowitz, the Deathlands novels.<br /> <br /> <br /> In which heroic badasses wander the wastelands between settlements battling warlords, mutants, and stranger things, while the Order of \u00c6on tries to rebuild civilization.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T14:04:29-07:00","id":1553883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1553875#post1553875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... <img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/joypixels/assets/8.0/png/unicode/64/1f914.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/joypixels/assets/8.0/png/unicode/64/1f914.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/joypixels/assets/8.0/png/unicode/64/1f914.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Apocalypse Then</b>, based on a bunch of the post-apocalyptic media of the 70s, 80s, and 90s.<br /> <br /> Primary Influences: The Road Warrior, Mad Max: Beyond Thunderdome, Thundarr the Barbarian, TMNT: After the Bomb, Cadillacs &amp; Dinosaurs, The Omega Man, Komandi, Tank Girl, Killraven, The Atomic Knights.<br /> <br /> Secondary Influences: Rifts, Terminator and Terminator 2, Damnation Alley, Logan's Run, Zardoz, the original Planet of the Apes franchise, Waterworld, The Postman, Cyborg, Six String Samurai, Hell Comes to Frogtown, 12 Monkeys, A Canticle for Leibowitz, the Deathlands novels.<br /> <br /> <br /> In which heroic badasses wander the wastelands between settlements battling warlords, mutants, and stranger things, while the Order of \u00c6on tries to rebuild civilization.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You read my mind. And improved my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-17T17:15:41-07:00","id":1553887,"title":"","content":"Factions for such a setting would probably include the Order of \u00c6on (the \u00c6on society as a quasireligious monastic order trying to rebuild civilization and preserve historical/scientific knowledge), some sort of network/guild of traveling merchants working to reestablish connections between different settlements, a loose army of monster hunters, and a faction focused on the burgeoning civilizations of uplifted animals and other sentient mutants. Not sure what else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T00:34:01-07:00","id":1553894,"title":"","content":"Another group could be focused on preventing inbreeding by getting isolated communities to exchange children. Those children growing up in their new communities and espousing the locals. (A secret faction in the group is really breeding homo superior mutants who look like normal humans and are better adapted to survive the post-apocalyptic world.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T08:06:53-07:00","id":1553900,"title":"","content":"It also needs some sort of order of psychic &quot;wizards&quot; akin to Thundarr's Princess Ariel and any similar characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T11:37:21-07:00","id":1553907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1553900#post1553900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also needs some sort of order of psychic &quot;wizards&quot; akin to Thundarr's Princess Ariel and any similar characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps one PC faction, morally neutral. And three minor factions, A) Wannabe Dark Lords, B) &quot;Holy&quot; wizards who are cold and unfriendly, probably &quot;witch hunters&quot; of PSIs they declare EVIL, and C) a monastic order of healers of the body and mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-18T15:48:39-07:00","id":1553912,"title":"","content":"The main Psi Wizards group should be a cross between a trade union (with apprenticeships and training), a professional group (maintaining standards and quality), and a lobbying group (demanding fair treatment and community respect). They'd object to group B as a threat. Group A would be looked down on and occasionally fought. Group C would be treated with respect and helped to get resources. <br /> <br /> The Healer Monastics would keep their distance from the Psi Wizards because it sees them as too worldly. But will cooperate to get resources needed to heal the sick in body and mind. The Dark Lord Wannabes are rejected, the Healer Monastics are pacifists and lean toward egalitarian ideals, the Dark Lord Wannabes are the total opposites. The Holy Wizards are feared. Their pogoms kill indiscriminately. <br /> <br /> The Dark Lord Wannabes try to work as a conspiracy. They mainly conspire against each other. The more successful members of the group try to infiltrate other groups and take them over. <br /> <br /> The Holy Wizards are fractious and hostile towards all outsiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T06:28:53-07:00","id":1553938,"title":"","content":"The <b>Daredevil</b> equivalents would be called <b>Seekers. </b>The kind of characters that were the protagonists in late 19th through to the 1980s in post-apocalyptic fiction were seeking something. Generally either their place in the world or answers to serious questions. Given the genre, <b>Stalwart </b>equivalents would be called <b>Mutants.</b> Although, as the book <b><i>Starman's Son </i></b>AKA <b><i>Daybreak 2250AD,</i></b> some novels did have mutant protagonists going through the quest process too. The <b>Mesmerist </b>equivalents could be called <b>Espers. </b>That term was very common in Golden Age Sci Fi and would cover both mystically inclined <b>Psis </b>and those with other worldviews.<br /> <br /> The <b>Mutants </b>should be able to gain extra powers through FLAWS a bit more dramatically than most PCs as a matter of genre. But not all mutants in these stories were deformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-20-2025, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T14:43:23-07:00","id":1553942,"title":"","content":"You could lift some ideas from the old Deadlands: Hell on Earth RPG, including calling Mesmerists <i>Psychers</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-20T21:16:36-07:00","id":1553951,"title":"","content":"Another pair of ideas the first would be a one-shot the second could be a series.<br /> <br /> The first one is <b>Airship. </b>Basically, it's an alternative 20th century were Airships were easy practical and highly durable. It's really a sea stories setting using Michael Moorcock's stories as inspiration. But I would blend in Bradbury as well. Picture any little Midwest town a skyport. Sailing to adventure escaping your drab little town. <br /> <br /> The second one is also an alternative 20th century which I call <b>ZEERUST. </b>Basically, a very Golden Age Sci Fi setting. Technology just speeds up. Moonbases in the 1950s. Mars bases in the 1960s. Exploration of the outer planets in the 1970s. It's the year 2000 and interstellar flight and exploration are starting. It's a retro Sci Fi setting, Talents and Psiads but no Quantum users ...known. <br /> <br /> Mars would be a dry world as in Bradbury's stories. There'd be ancient ruins to explore (think Northwest Smith). Envision little American towns in an exotic alien world sort of <b>Twilight Zone </b>meets <b>The Martian Chronicles. </b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-22T19:36:43-07:00","id":1553970,"title":"","content":"One really odd idea I keep wanting to explore, either in TC or some other action-adventure oriented system, is a world where a bunch of the crazy fictional continents exist. Mainly Atlantis and Mu, but probably a few others as well. This is mostly inspired by the YouTube channel Alternate History Hub's video about Mu (including its really crazy origins), especially about how such a massive continent in the Pacific likely would have resulted in Chinese contact with the Americas and the sort of impact that might have had. So by the same token, if there was a continent (probably smaller than Mu) in the middle of the Atlantic, would various pre-Rennaissance groups (the Basque, the Phoenicians, whomever) have founded settlements there and from there reached the Americas much earlier. And with such early contact and trade, could this avert the mass plagues that came with the Spanish. <br /> I'm thinking something along the lines of pulp fantasy (unless one wanted to go full \u00c6gis high fantasy) is an alternate 12th or 13th century, with various adventurers from around the world going from trading hub to trading hub, looking for fortune and glory, and finding mystery, danger, and wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-05T17:09:16-08:00","id":1558672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1553970#post1553970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One really odd idea I keep wanting to explore, either in TC or some other action-adventure oriented system, is a world where a bunch of the crazy fictional continents exist. Mainly Atlantis and Mu, but probably a few others as well. This is mostly inspired by the YouTube channel Alternate History Hub's video about Mu (including its really crazy origins), especially about how such a massive continent in the Pacific likely would have resulted in Chinese contact with the Americas and the sort of impact that might have had. So by the same token, if there was a continent (probably smaller than Mu) in the middle of the Atlantic, would various pre-Rennaissance groups (the Basque, the Phoenicians, whomever) have founded settlements there and from there reached the Americas much earlier. And with such early contact and trade, could this avert the mass plagues that came with the Spanish.<br /> I'm thinking something along the lines of pulp fantasy (unless one wanted to go full \u00c6gis high fantasy) is an alternate 12th or 13th century, with various adventurers from around the world going from trading hub to trading hub, looking for fortune and glory, and finding mystery, danger, and wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the idea of Pragmaclapses (relics left over from realities that now never existed) Atlantis and Mu might be erased realities struggling to return to our reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T15:42:37-07:00","id":1558808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1558672#post1558672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Using the idea of Pragmaclapses (relics left over from realities that now never existed) Atlantis and Mu might be erased realities struggling to return to our reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll note that Atlantis specifically exists in TC:Aegis, though I can't remember a lot of the details, aside from there being some sort of civilizational timeloop shenanigans going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28973-kenod","name":"kenod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T16:50:28-07:00","id":1558810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kenod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1558808#post1558808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll note that Atlantis specifically exists in TC:Aegis, though I can't remember a lot of the details, aside from there being some sort of civilizational timeloop shenanigans going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Helping or preventing Atlantis from escaping the timeloop could be epic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-25T12:08:51-07:00","id":1559619,"title":"","content":"A setting with three to five parallel worlds in conflict would be interesting. There's evidence that the parallels are merging. Each of the five wants to be the main/dominant reality. All the worlds diverged in the early 20th century and are experiencing the same year in the 21st century. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T14:57:08-08:00","id":1565089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kenod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1519165-your-tc-eras?p=1558808#post1558808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll note that Atlantis specifically exists in TC:Aegis, though I can't remember a lot of the details, aside from there being some sort of civilizational timeloop shenanigans going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just remembered that one trope in 1920s and 1930s pulp sci fi held that Atlantis was Mars. The Martians had a floating base in the Atlantic Ocean in one story (which I can't find). When civilization collapsed on Mars the base stopped getting regular maintenance so it degraded and sank.<br /> <br /> Having Atlantis be a misunderstood base for time travelers or space travelers. Plato placed Atlantis (which is total fiction in our reality) nine thousand years before his own time. That would place it before the seas were at the normal Holocene level. A time base on an island that was drowned in the Holocene oceanic rise would make a great Atlantis. <br /> <br /> Opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 11-02-2026, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-03T16:32:33-08:00","id":1565113,"title":"","content":"Anima and Aether both have the same otherdimensional threat invading the timeline, albeit in different ways. It wouldn't be inappropriate to extend that to Aegis as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}